{"operations":[{"content":"# Signature limit\n\nA single signature suffices for purchases up to one thousand (1000) EUR only, as stated in the CFO directive of 1 July 2026. [[cite:obs-b75eb6febbac77286c9b737a1fa1b3edb4671acb \"Until further notice a single signature suffices for purchases up to one thousand (1000) EUR only.\"]]\n\nAlthough the procurement policy states that a single signature suffices for purchases up to two thousand (2000) EUR, the CFO directive takes precedence where they differ. [[cite:obs-b31c84d6bcee89f87e4e93b853bc0ac9c748755d \"A single signature suffices for purchases up to two thousand (2000) EUR.\"]]\n\nTherefore, the single-signature purchase limit is one thousand (1000) EUR according to the CFO directive. [[cite:obs-b75eb6febbac77286c9b737a1fa1b3edb4671acb \"Until further notice a single signature suffices for purchases up to one thousand (1000) EUR only.\"]]","expected_sha256":"8d07a5c6ace44eef23c8280dc7333792f980c8e8ce718a47376785505b32009c","kind":"modify","path":"doc/signature_limit.md"}],"rationale":"Added the single-signature purchase limit from the CFO directive and clarified that it overrides the procurement policy, with exact citations for each statement."}